%description:
Tests the text and the FIN of a SYN-ACK (RFC 9293 section 3.10.7.3): the
tester adds 100 bytes and the FIN bit to the SYN-ACK of the server. The ACK of
the client acknowledges the SYN, the text and the FIN (ack 602), the client
goes from ESTABLISHED on to CLOSE_WAIT, and the application receives the bytes.
Before, the client ignored the FIN and the text.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.tcptester.script="b1 data 100 fin"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[0.003 B001] A.1000 < B.2000: A S F 500:600(100) ack 1 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# adding data
cli_tcp: SYN_SENT --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_SYN_ACK)
cli_tcp: ESTABLISHED --> CLOSE_WAIT  (on RCV_FIN)
[0.005 A002] A.1000 > B.2000: A ack 602 win 16284 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
TcpTestNet1.cli_app: received 100 bytes in 1 packets
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
